          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>According to the video, what is the most common cause of right heart failure in </p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>According to the video, what is the most common cause of right heart failure in everyday clinical practice?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Chronic lung disease (cor pulmonale)</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Cor pulmonale is the most common cause of isolated right heart failure, but overall, left heart failure causes more cases of right heart failure by overloading the right ventricle through raised pulmonary pressures.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Left heart failure</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. Congestion on the left side eventually raises pulmonary pressures and overloads the right ventricle, which is why biventricular failure is the most common pattern seen in practice.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Tricuspid valve disease</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Tricuspid valve disease can cause right heart failure, but it is far less common than the right ventricular overload that results from left heart failure.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Recurrent pulmonary embolism</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Pulmonary embolism can acutely strain the right ventricle, but it is not the most common cause of right heart failure in everyday clinical practice.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The video explained that while cor pulmonale is the leading cause of isolated right heart failure, the most common cause of right heart failure overall is left heart failure, because pulmonary congestion eventually overloads the right ventricle."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Exactly right. Left heart failure raises pulmonary pressures, which eventually overloads the right ventricle — that is why biventricular failure is the most common pattern."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
