          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>Which organism is most likely to cause acute infective endocarditis on a previou</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>Which organism is most likely to cause acute infective endocarditis on a previously normal heart valve?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Streptococcus viridans</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Streptococcus viridans classically causes subacute endocarditis on valves already damaged by conditions such as rheumatic heart disease, not on previously normal valves.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Enterococcus faecalis</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Enterococcus can cause endocarditis but typically points to a gut or urinary tract source and follows a more subacute course than Staphylococcus aureus.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Staphylococcus aureus</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. Staphylococcus aureus is virulent enough to infect previously normal valves, producing the fulminant acute form with high fever, rigors, and rapid valve destruction.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Streptococcus bovis</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Streptococcus bovis is associated with subacute endocarditis and carries an important link to colonic pathology — these patients always need a colonoscopy.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The video explained that Staphylococcus aureus is the organism virulent enough to attack previously normal valves, causing the acute fulminant form of infective endocarditis."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Exactly. S. aureus is uniquely virulent, capable of destroying even normal valves within days to weeks."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
